sentences.l:
and gave them to Deipylus, his dear comrade, whom beyond all
of his own age he honoured, because his mind was fitted to his own,
to drive to the hollow ships;

and straightway the spear pierced through the skin,
through the ambrosial robe, which for her the Graces themselves toiled to make,
at the base, above the palm;

and him Phoebus Apollo rescued in his hands
in a dark cloud, lest any of the swift-colted Danaans,
having cast bronze in his chest, should take his life from him;

And now there would have perished there Ares, insatiate of war,
if the stepmother, very fair Eeriboea,
had not told Hermes;

And Hera endured, when the strong son of Amphitryon
on the right breast with a three-barbed arrow
had struck her;

And Hades among them endured, huge, a swift arrow,
when that same man, the son of aegis-bearing Zeus,
at Pylos among the dead, having struck him, gave him to pains;
